# kwin_wayland

> KDE window manager.
> More information: <https://community.kde.org/KWin/Wayland>.

- Start KWin:

`kwin_wayland`

- Replace the currently running KWin:

`kwin_wayland --replace`

- Display help:

`kwin_wayland {{[-h|--help]}}`
